    "reservable": false,
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Ali Mohammadi",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/112906064637794431581/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjU4qBTbpOt0btR9YaDTNepQq-6TI_d3ylDF41P7wVHGK_UtIxnb=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
        "text": "Smoked Meat Pete is one of those places that feels timeless. We tried the classic smoked meat sandwich, the full rack of ribs, and the smoked meat poutine, and everything was excellent. The smoked meat is rich, tender, and full of flavour, easily among the best you can find in Montreal and the surrounding area. Honestly, if this place were located downtown, it would probably be considered the best smoked meat in Montreal.\n\nThe ribs were generous and well done, and the poutine with smoked meat was comforting and satisfying. Their coleslaw is also very good and pairs perfectly with the main dishes.\n\nThe atmosphere is friendly and welcoming, and you can really feel that this is a place people have been coming to for years. It’s always busy, especially in the summer when lineups are common, which says a lot. They also have a varied menu with things like pasta and ice cream, making it great for families and groups.\n\nIf you want to experience truly great smoked meat at a place that’s stood the test of time, Smoked Meat Pete is absolutely worth the trip.",
        "time": 1766547984,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Bill Bosley",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/110836573428638580632/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocItL_cim4YEyTkCaTbOHRkQ178epvxoNZoNdpvxVgof7j-nuQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
        "text": "First time here, from out of country. Recommended by a local friend, and I truly loved it. It was described as the best smoked meat, and it lived up to the expectation. Amazing smoked meat; good flavor, good texture, moist and tasty. Incredible ambience. Only down was I did not come on a night of live music which I saw the stage for. I really must come back to enjoy that, and especially get more smoked meat. I also enjoyed the poutine.",
        "time": 1763528047,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Karel",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/100216995710477716832/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjV5CpbWENe7vgFn78fR6kGUO30URahXvXsONOzlDq54nGEPeN8F=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba5",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "4 months ago",
        "text": "What a place!! 100% worth it! Probably the best smoked meat I’ve had around Montreal. The service is great and incredibly fast, even when the restaurant is full. The ambiance and the look of the place are just perfect! I’d go there every week if it were closer to my place. They even have a big stage for shows. Loved it! Enjoy 😎",
        "time": 1759702408,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Devildman",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/114102135268870799873/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjW0sWDXvNgtsw4PeZ9G6QObofyTQZB3Q9aN9y4BCu8g1NVXCclW=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "4 months ago",
        "text": "Excellent pit stop for smoke meat and barbecue food. The smoke meat poutine was sublime. The ribs marinade was so delicious (though somewhat dry meat).\nThe wait was about an hour in rush hour (2pm saturday), but was worth the wait.\nAmbience is really neat, I'm sure band nights must be great.\nAtmosphere gives me Nashville vibes.\n\nWill definitely return A+",
        "time": 1759169653,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Mark Sadkowski",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/105196518850680865261/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocKm-w_L_xKJGJg2g_sseZWsMu2BeDPd2sIirQ1hE2bLgPVzqg=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba6",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "3 months ago",
        "text": "Hey , montreal is known for really good food and really great culinary experience in many , many restaurants all over montreal.\nHowever Smoke Meat Pete is something that you will never forget.\nLocated on very West end of Montreal on an Island L'Ile Perrot.\nVery simple , to get to on highway twenty going west towards toronto , very first light that you ever encounter right there on the left hand side on an island.\nSimple restaurant , nothing fancy yet offers great experience that I have never had anything like that before.\nFirst of all, the way you order food, it's nothing like I've seen before.I'm not gonna go into details.You will find out yourself.\nSecond, at 4:30 PM on Sunday afternoon.It's not really dinner time yet.Yet ten minutes later after our arrival the place is super busy.\nPlenty of stuff to assist.You put a ride in fasthey're writing a fast method.Really?It's not a high-end restaurant.What matters is the smoke meats?They have it done to perfection iver the years.\nAnd then an hour or so later.We have a live band playing music.Bluees mostly.\nAt 7 PM, all tables are takand mostly rather retired crowd.Listening to the band playing and they are people still flowing in to the access dining space that they have.\nVery , very unique experience , especially if you're not from montreal.",
        "time": 1762395623,
        "translated": false
      }
    ],
